server.detail:
Body: {question_id, answer, ms, guess?: bool}. cfg['ms'][qid] accumulates ms across visits.

instant: as today, plus the response adds:
- reasons: a per-option list, with '' for the key;
- accepted: for SPR, from scoring.accepted_forms;
- status;
- pace: {ms, type_avg_ms}.

retry: the first try claims the answer (set_answer only_new) and files the attempt as today. A wrong first try returns {correct:false, final:false, mistake, given, tries_left:2}, with no answer, answer_index or rationale. Later tries on the same qid:
- are written to the new tries table;
- file a trap hit when their reason names a mistake (progress.record_trap);
- return final:true with full feedback when right or when tries run out;
- make the question 'mixed' when it ends right.

end:
- set_answer without only_new, so an answer can be changed;
- nothing is filed until finish;
- the response is {saved:true, answered}, with no feedback keys.

guess=true stores attempts.guess=1.

finish() adds:
- mixed, skipped, unanswered;
- accuracy (first try);
- avg_ms and pace: 95;
- by_difficulty: {easy:{right,asked},...};
- levels_seen: [min, max];
- guessed_right;
- questions: [{id, n, topic, skill, difficulty, level, status, ms, mistake, marked, repair, guess}];
- fix: the count of missed templates.

In end mode it first files every answered question through progress.record (in order, with cfg['ms']), then computes opened and closed as today. It keeps 'one attempt per question, the first' for the counts.

Add checks for:
- /api/bank totals (4/19/386);
- the formats and levels filters;
- the 409 on an unservable selection;
- templates-only sets;
- skip then answer later;
- retry mode hiding the key until final, and 'mixed' in finish;
- end mode leaking nothing before finish, and filing at finish;
- more growing the total, with the same template on a new seed;
- pause freezing seconds_left;
- retake giving identical stems in order;
- share giving identical stems to a second learner;
